      "side": 1,
      "message": "With this pattern there\u0027s some QueryTasks that have outdated servicesToResolve and sendDiscoveryQueries values (when created in scheduleNextRun), but they\u0027re recreated before running.\n\nI think you actually want to have a separate ScheduledQueryTask data object to schedule the query, and a QueryTaskRunnable that is actually posted.\n\nSo maybe you could do things like:\n\n```\nprivate static class ScheduledQueryTask {\n    private final QueryTaskConfig config;\n    private final long timeToRun;\n    private final long minTtlExpirationTimeWhenScheduled;\n    private final long sessionId;\n}\n\nprivate static class QueryTaskRunnable implements Runnable {\n    private final ScheduledQueryTask scheduledTask;\n    private final List\u003cMdnsResponse\u003e servicesToResolve;\n    private final boolean sendDiscoveryQueries;\n    private final Handler postResultHandler;\n    \n    @Override\n    public void run() {\n        final Pair\u003cInteger, List\u003cString\u003e\u003e result \u003d\n            new EnqueueMdnsQueryCallable(...).call();\n        postResultHandler.postMessage(postResultHandler.obtainMessage(\n            EVENT_QUERY_SENT, new QuerySentResult(result, scheduledTask)));\n    }\n    \n}\n```",
      "revId": "71e5821c3b89d95c8bc42c7007b810339aa6cd28",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
